  "title": "Arrow vs function",
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "explain",
      "md": "## Shorter is not the whole story\n\n`const add = (a, b) => a + b` is shorter. An arrow also **does not get its own `this`**. It keeps the `this` from outside.\n\nA method that needs `this.dir` should stay a `function`, or you bind it later. This lesson is syntax plus that preview — no DOM yet."
    },
    {
